  "id": "openai-responses-proxy",
  "locale": "en",
  "title": "OpenAI Responses Proxy",
  "question": "How does OpenAI Responses Proxy make a Codex Responses turn portable across third-party providers, and how does it install and keep its own listener running?",
  "summary": "A loopback listener rebuilds each Responses request in one closed grammar with store=false, sends it to the provider its path names within one total deadline, and retries only what the failure class allows. A signed release installs through one journaled transaction as an immutable generation; an upgrade hands the listening socket to the new process, and a watchdog under the native service manager restarts a stopped listener.",
  "scope": "The OpenAI Responses Proxy product as released at v5.1.10: the openai_responses_proxy package with its provider manifest, pyproject.toml and VERSION.",
  "limits": [
    "Each component owns the files its claims name; a relation cites the files that import or call the other component.",
    "A relation stands for an import, a call on an object of the other component that the caller hands over, or a process call that carries behaviour; imports used only for an exception class, a type, a shared helper or the product's names are not drawn.",
    "Tests, the repository tools, the OpenSpec specifications and change history, the documents and CI are outside the scope, each excluded with its reason."
  ],
